On the western side of the Le Morne peninsula the public beach is one of the most beautiful on the island. It has fine white sand and a lagoon of clear shallow water with the cliffs of Le Morne Brabant rising directly behind it.

The lagoon off the peninsula is also one of the world's best known places for kitesurfing so on windy days the sky fills with kites further along the shore.

Just inland from the beach stands the Slave Route Monument.

## Good to know

- Shade is limited: bring a parasol or come early or late in the day.
- Kitesurfers use parts of the lagoon. Swim where others swim and away from their launch areas.
